<h2>Content pages</h2>
<p>Under <strong>Administration → Pages</strong>, pages such as the imprint, terms, privacy policy, withdrawal and report forms are made. A page has a language per text, a status (draft or published), a place in the header or footer, and can carry one of the legal roles. A legal role exists only once: only one page can be the imprint.</p>
<p>A language with no text of its own shows the default language's text.</p>

<h2>Media library</h2>
<p>Under <strong>Administration → Media library</strong>, pictures for the site are uploaded: JPEG, PNG or WebP up to 8 MB. Each picture is saved again (metadata removed, pictures over 2400 pixels scaled down) and gets a fixed address. The picker next to a text field inserts pictures from the library into page texts.</p>

<h2>Editing the home and offer page in place</h2>
<p>The home page - and, where a catalogue extension is running, the offer page - are made of blocks: a title area, text, latest offers, top providers, a picture, a link list. These blocks can be edited right on the page itself, not only through a form in the administration: a click on a text makes it editable, a "+" between two blocks inserts a new one. Blocks can be moved, hidden, removed, added and duplicated. A block used often can be saved as a widget of its own and inserted again later.</p>
<p>Texts are edited in whichever language the header currently shows; the other languages stay as they are. Anyone who prefers a form instead finds the same blocks under <strong>Administration → Home page</strong> and <strong>Offer page</strong>.</p>

<h2>Design</h2>
<p>Under <strong>Administration → Design</strong>, the accent colour, background, text colour, font (four system font families) and corner radius are set. These values go into a small stylesheet of their own; the templates themselves stay untouched. The colours apply to the light colour scheme. The logo and the favicon are under <strong>Themes → Branding</strong>.</p>
